From aed364af278a26e71d34ecfa3569ea870e82ccfb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 12:28:25 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] policy: compute local admission fees on a node-owned worker

Move mempool backlog updates into a bounded multi-producer queue. On overflow evict older absolute-total samples to retain the newest total without lost-delta accounting drift. Publish the independent admission scalar through a relaxed atomic, and cache coherent RPC diagnostics separately. Leave authoritative chain-history EMA and adaptive consensus capacity synchronous; generation tags discard queued local samples from before a reorg/reset.

Initialize the worker during AppInitMain, before mempool producers start, and drain/join after producer teardown. Successful sendrawtransaction and admission do not scan fee history. Add behavioral coverage for calculation-lock independence, online parity, queue overflow, generation reset with and without new producers, concurrent producers and worker shutdown. Validation pending coordinated incremental build.
